Wed Oct 21 22:30:00 UTC 2026 - tokajer <tokajer@tokajer.at>

- The root helper is split into modules (check, update, snapshots).
- After the update the kernel modules and the default boot entry are
  handled by nazoos-common directly; a failure there is only a note.
- Details window uses the shared log view.

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Wed Oct 21 20:30:00 UTC 2026 - tokajer <tokajer@tokajer.at>

- Starting NazoOS Update again (menu, KRunner, a notification) brings
  the open window to the front instead of opening another one.

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Wed Oct 21 12:00:00 UTC 2026 - tokajer <tokajer@tokajer.at>

- The package list keeps package names readable and shortens long
  versions from the left instead, so the new version stays visible.
- The details window follows new output like a terminal, unless it
  was scrolled up to read.
- The boot menu names of an update's snapshots are no longer
  overwritten with "software change" by the background naming run.
- The summary no longer says "up to date" when the check failed or the
  update needs a decision.
- Dependency problems are shown without zypper's "Detailed
  information" prefix.
- "Check now" no longer opens an error dialog on top of the warning
  that already explains the conflict or the connection problem.

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Tue Oct 20 12:00:00 UTC 2026 - tokajer <tokajer@tokajer.at>

- The restart notice is no longer shown for plasma packages that are
  not part of the desktop.
- An update conflict now shows the actual problem instead of a
  generic message.
- The Myrlyn hint names the Dist-Upgrade view where the conflict
  can be resolved.
- Neutral icon instead of a green check before the first check.

