- Notifications 10 s after login with AccuracySec=1s (the timer's
  default accuracy of 1 min made it fire up to a minute late)

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Sun Oct 11 21:30:00 UTC 2026 - tokajer <tokajer@tokajer.at>

- Rollback: detect a snapshot booted from GRUB by the read-only flag
  of the btrfs subvolume; it is mounted "rw", so the notification and
  "Make permanent" never appeared
- Boot menu: readable snapshot names via snapper userdata "bootloader"
  ("Before update", "After software change", "Automatic snapshot",
  with local date, in the system language) instead of
  "kernel,date,pre,zypp(zypper)"
- No downgrades: when the mirrors still have an older Tumbleweed
  snapshot than the system, show a note instead of offering a
  "dist-upgrade" back to it; "Update now" then only updates Flatpaks
- Starting with sudo: clear message instead of a Qt platform error
- Hide the "Done." message when the next action starts
- Notifications 30 s after login instead of 2 min (snapshot notice)
- Buttons in notifications: start the window in its own systemd unit;
  as a child of the oneshot notify service it was killed right away
- "Make permanent" from the notification: open the question only once
  the window is shown

